{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/145806-game-set-in-arcadia","id":145806,"title":"Game Set in Arcadia","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-22T10:39:31-07:00","id":145806,"title":"Game Set in Arcadia","content":"I'm currently DMing a changeling game set in my home town. Rather than have my players start as changelings, I started them as mortals and through some rather horrible story arcs pulled them into Arcadia. I had them make up a bunch of fey titles, and through play they each got assigned a keeper based on someone else's titles (one person ended up with a winter fey of pain and darkness, which hasn't turned out well for her) I've been pulling a lot of source from equinox road and dancers in the dusk, but I'm on the constant lookout for more. Can anyone recommend any good books or additional source material? Which books would have the best information for games set in Arcadia? So far my players love it to death 20 or so games in, but I would still like more curveballs to throw at them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3092-felidaeus","name":"Felidaeus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T14:48:17-07:00","id":146058,"title":"","content":"Equinox Road. That will have pretty much exactly what you are looking for. Well kind of, it talks about the end game for changeling and how one would seek out Arcadia and maybe what one could do when one get's there but I suspect there are some pretty good ideas in the book that might give you some inspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T15:34:34-07:00","id":146094,"title":"","content":"The whole thing of the players coming up with titles and those titles becoming another player's Keeper is rather neat. It also puts me in the mind of Wraith, where you played each others' Shadows. I'm not sure about the idea of going that path, but it's an idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2546-jaellot","name":"jaellot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2546_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}